	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;div&gt;The Chief Election Commissioner is &lt;strong&gt;appointed by the President&lt;/strong&gt; and the &lt;strong&gt;other Election Commissioners are appointed by the President after consultation with the Chief Election Commissioner,&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Article 324 &lt;/strong&gt;also provides for the appointment of Regional Commissioners at the time of General Elections after consultation with the Election Commission.&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
