	&lt;li&gt;रोगी की सुरक्षा सुनिश्चित करने और जोखिमों को कम करने के लिए, यांत्रिक वेंटिलेशन पर रोगियों में प्रत्येक सक्शन प्रयास के लिए अनुशंसित अवधि 5 - 10 सेकंड है। इससे हाइपोक्सिमिया को रोकने में मदद मिलती है और अन्य जटिलताओं के होने की संभावना कम हो जाती है।&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

en.value:
&lt;div&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Correct Answer: Sit for 5 minutes before standing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rationale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Patients on antihypertensive medications can experience orthostatic hypotension, which is a sudden drop in blood pressure upon standing that can cause dizziness and lightheadedness. Advising patients to sit for 5 minutes before standing helps their bodies adjust to the change in position and can prevent these symptoms.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Explanation of Other Options:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Wear support hose continuously&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Rationale: While wearing support hose can help improve circulation and reduce the risk of blood pooling in the legs, it is not specifically targeted at preventing the transient dizziness and lightheadedness caused by orthostatic hypotension.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Lie down for 15 minutes after taking medication&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Rationale: Lying down after taking medication is not a practical or necessary solution for managing orthostatic hypotension. It also does not address the act of transitioning from lying to standing, which is when orthostatic hypotension typically occurs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Avoid exercise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Rationale: Avoiding exercise is not beneficial advice. Regular exercise is important for overall cardiovascular health and can actually help reduce blood pressure in the long term. Patients should instead be advised on how to safely manage their symptoms when changing positions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conclusion&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Sitting for 5 minutes before standing allows the body to equalize blood pressure, helping to prevent dizziness and lightheadedness associated with orthostatic hypotension in patients taking antihypertensive medications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

